<title>UK: World Bank adds 500 bln lire to zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank adds 500 bln lire to zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers Citibank and Credito Italiano.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT ** 1.5 TRLN ITL  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    07.NOV.16</p>
<p> TYPE   ZERO-COUPON   ISS PRICE  23.16     PAY DATE    07.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> NOTES   ** ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 1.0 TRLN LIRE ON 02.OCT.96</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50-500  SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  1.85</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF A GLOBAL MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
